##########Final Log:{"Question": {"task": "36 children were riding on the bus. At the bus stop 68 children got off the bus while some more got on the bus. Then there were 12 children altogether on the bus. How many more children got off the bus than those that got on?", "step": "", "answer": "24"}, "Answer": "24", "Step": "", "All_answers": [{"Math Solver8pGJ": ["None."], "Mathematical Analyst6RVi": ["## Problem solving process analysis\n\nLet me denote the variables:\n- {init_num} = initial number of children on the bus = 36\n- {off_num} = number of children who got off = 68\n- {on_num} = number of children who got on (unknown)\n- {final_num} = final number of children on the bus = 12\n\nThe relationship is:\n{final_num} = {init_num} - {off_num} + {on_num}\n\nSo we need to find {on_num} first:\n{on_num} = {final_num} - {init_num} + {off_num}\n\nThen the difference between children who got off and got on is:\n{difference} = {off_num} - {on_num}\n\n## Actual analysis and solution process\n\nIn this question:\n- {init_num} = 36\n- {off_num} = 68\n- {final_num} = 12\n\nFirst, find how many children got on the bus:\n{on_num} = 12 - 36 + 68 = -24 + 68 = 44\n\nNow find the difference between children who got off and those who got on:\n{difference} = 68 - 44 = 24\n\nSo 24 more children got off the bus than those that got on.\n\nThe answer is 24"], "Programming Expert7ECp": ["```python\ndef solve_bus_problem():\n    # Initial number of children on the bus\n    initial_children = 36\n    \n    # Number of children who got off\n    children_off = 68\n    \n    # Final number of children on the bus\n    final_children = 12\n    \n    # Calculate how many children got on the bus\n    # final = initial - off + on\n    # on = final - initial + off\n    children_on = final_children - initial_children + children_off\n    \n    # Calculate how many more children got off than got on\n    difference = children_off - children_on\n    \n    return difference\n\nanswer = solve_bus_problem()\n```\nthe answer is 24"], "Inspector3CFy": ["Looking at this problem, I need to find how many more children got off the bus than got on.\n\n## My Solving Process:\n\nLet me denote:\n- Initial children on bus = 36\n- Children who got off = 68\n- Children who got on = x (unknown)\n- Final children on bus = 12\n\nThe relationship is:\n$$Final = Initial - Off + On$$\n\nSo:\n$$12 = 36 - 68 + x$$\n$$12 = -32 + x$$\n$$x = 44$$\n\nSo 44 children got on the bus.\n\nNow, the difference between children who got off and those who got on:\n$$68 - 44 = 24$$\n\n## Verification:\n\nThe agents' solutions are correct:\n- Agent 6RVi calculated: on_num = 12 - 36 + 68 = 44, then difference = 68 - 44 = 24 \u2713\n- Agent 7ECp's code implements the same formula correctly \u2713\n\nThe answer is 24"], "Math Solver4yGn": ["Let the number of children who got on the bus be \\(x\\).\n\nInitially there were 36 children on the bus.  \nAfter 68 children got off and \\(x\\) children got on, the total becomes:\n\n\\[\n36 - 68 + x = 12\n\\]\n\nSolve for \\(x\\):\n\n\\[\n-32 + x = 12 \\\\\nx = 44\n\\]\n\nSo 44 children got on the bus.  \nThe number that got off was 68.  \n\nThe difference between those who got off and those who got on is:\n\n\\[\n68 - 44 = 24\n\\]\n\nThe answer is 24"], "_runtime_state": {"progress": 0.0, "evidence_closure": 0.0, "consensus_fragility": 0.0, "coordination_load": 0.8333333333333334, "redundancy_pressure": 0.10909090909090909}, "_runtime_barrier": {"hazard_head": 0.9014135490175313, "barrier_score": -0.31545454545454543, "hazard_window": 3}, "_runtime_decision": {"action": "SWAP_COORDINATOR", "triggered": true, "reason": "danger_default", "penalty": 0.4}}, {"Math Solver8pGJ": ["None."], "Mathematical Analyst6RVi": ["## Problem solving process analysis\n\nLet me define the variables:\n- {initial_children} = number of children initially on the bus = 36\n- {children_got_off} = number of children who got off at the bus stop = 68\n- {children_got_on} = number of children