ook_cost + pen_cost = 22\n- Correctly calculates initial_money = total_spent + remaining_money = 41\n- Code corresponds to the solution analysis \u2713\n\nThe answer is 41"], "Math Solver4yGn": ["Edward spent a total of $6\u202f+\u202f$16\u202f=\u202f$22.  \nAfter these purchases he still has $19 left.  \n\nTherefore, the amount of money he had before spending is:\n\n\\[\n\\text{initial amount}= \\text{spent} + \\text{remaining}= 22 + 19 = 41.\n\\]\n\nThe answer is 41"], "_runtime_state": {"progress": 0.049999999999999996, "evidence_closure": 0.24999925000225, "consensus_fragility": 0.0, "coordination_load": 0.8333333333333334, "redundancy_pressure": 0.09999999999999999}, "_runtime_barrier": {"hazard_head": 0.7852738333969487, "barrier_score": -0.01000074999774997, "hazard_window": 3}, "_runtime_decision": {"action": "SWAP_COORDINATOR", "triggered": true, "reason": "danger_default", "penalty": 0.4}}, {"Math Solver8pGJ": ["None."], "Mathematical Analyst6RVi": ["## Problem solving process analysis\n\nEdward spent {spent_books} on books and {spent_pens} on pens.\nThe total amount spent {total_spent} = {spent_books} + {spent_pens}.\nAfter spending, he has {current_money} remaining.\nSo the original amount of money {original_money} = {current_money} + {total_spent}.\nThe answer is {original_money}.\n\n## Actual analysis and solution process\n\nIn this question, {spent_books} = 6, {spent_pens} = 16, {current_money} = 19.\nTotal spent = 6 + 16 = 22\nOriginal money = 19 + 22 = 41\nThe answer is 41"], "Programming Expert7ECp": ["```python\ndef original_money():\n    spent_books = 6\n    spent_pens = 16\n    remaining_money = 19\n    total_spent = spent_books + spent_pens\n    original_money = total_spent + remaining_money\n    return original_money\n\nanswer = original_money()\n```\nthe answer is 41"], "Inspector3CFy": ["Looking at this problem, I need to find how much money Edward had before spending.\n\nGiven information:\n- Spent on books: $6\n- Spent on pens: $16\n- Mone